# Managed QA user (Rule 22, qa-005). Copy to apps/web/.qa.env (gitignored) and fill in.
# Never commit .qa.env, never paste the password or the TOTP secret into a PR, a doc,
# a chat or project memory. Memory holds only: the username (QA_ADMIN_EMAIL) and the
# path of this file.
#
# Local stack: `npm run qa:user` creates the user and writes .qa.env for you.
# DEV / PROD: the user is created by Yuval (the accounts are hers) or by Ran with her
# go-ahead, in her Supabase project: an Auth user with a long random password, a row in
# `admins`, and a TOTP factor whose secret is kept here so a test can pass the code step.
# One QA user per environment; remove it (Auth user + admins row) when the tests stop.

# Where the user lives: local | dev | prod
QA_ENV=
# The site the user logs in to, e.g. http://localhost:3100 or the DEV url
QA_BASE_URL=
# Admin QA user (the login at /admin/login)
QA_ADMIN_EMAIL=
QA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# Base32 TOTP secret of the user's verified factor (what the QR code encodes)
QA_ADMIN_TOTP_SECRET=
